(*
MagTagChordNode — proves CHORDING ("hold A, press B") on the MagTag without a
level-read prim and without any VM change.

HOW IT WORKS. zephyr/src/main.c's debounced button state machine fires TWO logical
pins per button: the press on the button's GPIO number, and the settled release on
GPIO + OEVM_BUTTON_RELEASE_BASE (100). A logical pin is nothing more than a key
into src/platform.c's host_gpio_register table, so a second key per button costs a
table slot and no new primitive. This node registers both, keeps a held-flag per
button, and prints the whole held set on every transition — so a chord is visible
directly in the console.

  BUTTON_A  press 15   release 115
  BUTTON_B  press 14   release 114
  BUTTON_C  press 12   release 112
  BUTTON_D  press 11   release 111

WHY NOT A LEVEL READ. The design doc's preferred long-term answer is a
`gpio level: n` primitive — chording then costs ZERO mailbox traffic, because the
node asks only when it cares. Release events are the cheaper thing to TEST, since
they need no cross-repo prim append, but they do double the event rate. If chording
becomes a real feature rather than an experiment, revisit
docs/design/2026-07-23-magtag-buttons-leds-design.md's "Deferred" section.

RELEASE EVENTS COST NOTHING WHEN UNUSED, which is why main.c fires them
unconditionally: host_gpio_fire walks the registration table and posts only for
pins some node registered, so the nRF boards (which register 13 and never 113) see
no change at all.

DEBOUNCE APPLIES TO BOTH EDGES, so a held button is a *settled* held button — the
flags cannot flutter during contact bounce. That is what makes the held set
trustworthy enough to test a chord against.

expect — press A, keep holding, then press and release B, then release A:
A down   held=A
B down   held=AB
B up     held=A
A up     held=
*)
class MagTagChordNode packageUsing: manifest = (
  | aHeld ::= false. bHeld ::= false. cHeld ::= false. dHeld ::= false. |
) (
  heldSet = (
    | s |
    s:: ''.
    aHeld ifTrue: [ s:: s , 'A' ].
    bHeld ifTrue: [ s:: s , 'B' ].
    cHeld ifTrue: [ s:: s , 'C' ].
    dHeld ifTrue: [ s:: s , 'D' ].
    ^ s
  )

  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space gpio aDn aUp bDn bUp cDn cUp dDn dUp |
    space:: platform space.

    aDn:: space channel: 'btn/a/down'.  aUp:: space channel: 'btn/a/up'.
    bDn:: space channel: 'btn/b/down'.  bUp:: space channel: 'btn/b/up'.
    cDn:: space channel: 'btn/c/down'.  cUp:: space channel: 'btn/c/up'.
    dDn:: space channel: 'btn/d/down'.  dUp:: space channel: 'btn/d/up'.

    aDn whenever: '' do: [ :m | aHeld:: true.  ('A down   held=' , self heldSet) println ].
    aUp whenever: '' do: [ :m | aHeld:: false. ('A up     held=' , self heldSet) println ].
    bDn whenever: '' do: [ :m | bHeld:: true.  ('B down   held=' , self heldSet) println ].
    bUp whenever: '' do: [ :m | bHeld:: false. ('B up     held=' , self heldSet) println ].
    cDn whenever: '' do: [ :m | cHeld:: true.  ('C down   held=' , self heldSet) println ].
    cUp whenever: '' do: [ :m | cHeld:: false. ('C up     held=' , self heldSet) println ].
    dDn whenever: '' do: [ :m | dHeld:: true.  ('D down   held=' , self heldSet) println ].
    dUp whenever: '' do: [ :m | dHeld:: false. ('D up     held=' , self heldSet) println ].

    gpio:: platform gpio.
    gpio pin:  15 edge: #falling post: 'A' on: aDn.
    gpio pin: 115 edge: #rising  post: 'A' on: aUp.
    gpio pin:  14 edge: #falling post: 'B' on: bDn.
    gpio pin: 114 edge: #rising  post: 'B' on: bUp.
    gpio pin:  12 edge: #falling post: 'C' on: cDn.
    gpio pin: 112 edge: #rising  post: 'C' on: cUp.
    gpio pin:  11 edge: #falling post: 'D' on: dDn.
    gpio pin: 111 edge: #rising  post: 'D' on: dUp.

    [ true ] whileTrue: [ platform pumpEvents. space drain ]
  )
) : (
)
